{"engine_version":"0.28.0","file":"campaign-monte-carlo-clock-holdover.toml","toml":"# A seeded Monte Carlo ensemble through a campaign, on a case with a closed form.\n#\n# A chip-scale atomic clock (Microchip SA.45s datasheet sigma_y(1 s) = 3e-10, so a\n# white-frequency-noise intensity q_wf = 9e-20 s^2/s and nothing else stochastic) is\n# disciplined to GNSS for 600 s and then coasts to 3600 s. The holdover predictor\n# removes the deterministic frequency offset exactly, so the time error at the end\n# of the run is the accumulated white-frequency noise since the last synchronisation\n# at 590 s: Gaussian, mean zero, variance q_wf * tau with tau = 3010 s, a standard\n# deviation of sqrt(9e-20 * 3010) s = 16.46 ns (NIST Technical Note 1337, the random\n# walk of phase under white frequency noise).\n#\n# Realisation k runs the scenario with `seed = 42 + k`, so the ensemble reproduces\n# exactly. The campaign reports, per metric, the mean, the standard deviation, the\n# 5th, 50th and 95th percentiles and a fixed-seed bootstrap 95% confidence interval\n# on the mean. The test suite checks that the mean falls inside that interval around\n# zero and that the spread matches 16.46 ns.\n#\n# MODELLED: the clock is a datasheet-level model, not a measurement of any unit.\nkind = \"campaign\"\ntitle = \"Monte Carlo: free-running clock error against its closed form\"\nseed = 20260928\n\n[monte_carlo]\nruns = 200\nseed_key = \"seed\"\nmetrics = [\n  { name = \"final_error\", path = \"classical.series[-1].error_ns\" },\n  { name = \"timing_rms\", path = \"classical.fom.timing_rms_ns\" },\n]\n\n[monte_carlo.scenario]\nseed = 42\nthreshold_ns = 20.0\n[monte_carlo.scenario.time]\nstep_s = 10.0\nduration_s = 3600.0\n[monte_carlo.scenario.gnss]\nwindows = [\n  { t0 = 0.0, t1 = 600.0, state = \"nominal\" },\n  { t0 = 600.0, t1 = 3600.0, state = \"denied\" },\n]\n[monte_carlo.scenario.clock_quantum]\nid = \"optical-sr-lattice\"\nprovenance = \"Strontium optical lattice clock, space-oriented goal sigma_y(1s)=1e-15 (arXiv:1503.08457); not flown.\"\ny0 = 5.0e-17\nq_wf = 1.0e-30\nq_rw = 0.0\n[monte_carlo.scenario.clock_classical]\nid = \"csac-sa45s\"\nprovenance = \"Microchip SA65 / SA.45s CSAC datasheet sigma_y(1s)=3e-10; q_wf=sigma_y(1s)^2.\"\ny0 = 5.0e-10\nq_wf = 9.0e-20\nq_rw = 0.0\n","summary":"campaign e093a8c2f169 | Monte Carlo: free-running clock error against its closed form | monte carlo of `clock`: 200 seeds | 200 member runs (MODELLED)","json":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"0.7\",\n  \"engine_version\": \"0.28.0\",\n  \"scenario_hash\": \"e093a8c2f16933f42eb97c22ff3029df9f50928f31da237318de06ff84444dfd\",\n  \"seed\": 20260928,\n  \"kind\": \"campaign\",\n  \"title\": \"Monte Carlo: free-running clock error against its closed form\",\n  \"label\": \"MODELLED composition of existing scenario kinds. Every number is read from a real run of the named kind; the chaining (additive carry of a channel across a phase boundary, zero-order hold onto the timeline grid, a phase ended at a computed time) is a modelling choice, and each phase carries the label of the kind that produced it.\",\n  \"reproducibility\": {\n    \"campaign_hash\": \"e093a8c2f16933f42eb97c22ff3029df9f50928f31da237318de06ff84444dfd\",\n    \"runs_total\": 200,\n    \"run_digest\": \"283a3873ec27d76415ef4e29bc666e94c3bfa68b97c8c0c0db44aa5e3ff84892\"\n  },\n  \"monte_carlo\": {\n    \"scenario_kind\": \"clock\",\n    \"runs\": 200,\n    \"seed_key\": \"seed\",\n    \"base_seed\": 42,\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"final_error\": {\n        \"path\": \"classical.series[-1].error_ns\",\n        \"unit\": \"ns\",\n        \"n\": 200,\n        \"mean\": -0.45362071346961735,\n        \"std\": 14.926503004916897,\n        \"p05\": -24.9472448938487,\n        \"p50\": 0.8579374379226544,\n        \"p95\": 24.44881251860626,\n        \"ci95_low\": -2.518450541106308,\n        \"ci95_high\": 1.590336442566398,\n        \"samples\": [\n          23.18836200405387,\n          3.3579007028363916